{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204765-the-technocracy-and-the-star-wars-prequels","id":1204765,"title":"The Technocracy and the Star Wars prequels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-08T19:24:12-07:00","id":1204765,"title":"The Technocracy and the Star Wars prequels","content":"Is the focus on Nephandic infiltration of the Technocracy inspired by the Star Wars prequels? I mean, an establishment group beats a rebel group, only for the establishment group to have been corrupted from the inside by the ultimate evil? Am I describing the Technocracy or the Republic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T19:34:22-07:00","id":1204766,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a fairly common trope, so I wouldn\u2019t say it was inspired by Star Wars, but that they had similar leanings, if rather different in scope and execution.<br /> <br /> The idea of infiltration and slow corruption has been around for a while as a way of explaining how the once novel became ignoble without assigning blame to the establishment itself. See the rise of Stalinism on the ideals of the communist revolution for an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T19:36:33-07:00","id":1204767,"title":"","content":"You do realize that the Star Wars prequel series were written years after Mage the Ascension, right? Goodness I hope you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T19:43:54-07:00","id":1204769,"title":"","content":"Yes, I know that. But the focus on the Neph corrupting the Technocracy rather than the Technocracy having inherently evil goals has been recent. And there was no need to troll me about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T03:22:00-07:00","id":1204824,"title":"","content":"I was not attempting to troll. It was a legitimate concern because from my perspective your question seemed kind of silly, and possibly like YOU were trolling. Good to see that is not the case. <br /> <br /> As far as nephandic infiltration of the technocracy being a recent change... well no it isn't. It has been established since at least revised edition and that was printed in 2000. While it is more recent than 2nd - which was 1995 - there are people who were born that year and are now considered legal adults.<br /> <br /> Of the prequel trilogy, only The Phantom Menace came before revised edition of Mage. I don't think there's a correlation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","user":"PazuzuAxelf","date":". 04-09-2018, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T06:48:32-07:00","id":1204846,"title":"","content":"Nephandi infiltration was going on well before the Rev Ed. The original Convention Book for the VE had it's first two chapters revolve around a VE, Dana Gardener, explaining the Convention and it's history only to reveal at the end that she's Nephandi. Because even back then WW realized that the VE were too good for the rest of the Union and tried to find a way to darken the Convention to better match their peers. Being corrupted by the alien horrors they encountered in the Void was what they came up with at the time.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's been around for quite some time and honestly it makes sense that the Nephandi would be infiltrating the Technocracy and the Traditions for the matter. The Nephandi subvert and corrupt. Doing that to the two biggest groups of MtAs would be a natural fit for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:46:36-07:00","id":1206399,"title":"","content":"So, which book reveals that Awakening is caused by a high concentration of midichlorians in your bloodstream?<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't laugh, I honestly wouldn't put it past the Technocracy to try something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-13-2018, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}